{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender","id":248635,"title":"B&S Red Surrender","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-03T23:18:01-07:00","id":248635,"title":"B&S Red Surrender","content":"Has it been discussed and will it make a return? <br /> <br /> Always thought it was an interesting thing and was toying with a coil based around the premise of the characters higher mind and the beast working together to improve their survival. <br /> <br /> Just curious. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T00:32:14-07:00","id":248681,"title":"","content":"Haven't seen any sort of discussions whatsoever, but I think I'd love to figure out some updates to the Red Surrender for B&amp;S. The idea of it is awesome, however execution was not the best... I'd like Red Surrender to have advantages and disadvantages.. and sadly the old version of it had no disadvantages for some concepts (and no advantages for others)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T01:40:44-07:00","id":248699,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">From my game: </span><br /> <br /> Red Surrender Conditions</span><br /> At any time, when a Gangrel successfully resists frenzy, she can choose to enter the Crescent Moon phase of Red Surrender. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Surrender (New Moon)</span><br /> Your character has shaken off the Red Surrender. In beating back her Beast, the monster within has grown docile and complacent like a domesticated animal. Add five dice to any roll to resist frenzy. Subtract one from her effective Blood Potency. Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Survival, and Weaponry rolls do not benefit from the 10-again quality. <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Lose Humanity. Enter torpor. Commit Amaranth. Suffer a wound penalty from aggravated damage. <br /> <b>Note:</b> If your character enters New Moon Surrender while in torpor during Full Moon Surrender, calculate her torpor time as if her Humanity were two dots lower, and her Blood Potency two dots higher. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Surrender (Crescent Moon)</span><br /> Your character has chosen to let her Beast ride along as copilot. Subtract one die from any rolls to resist frenzy. She gains the 9-again quality on all Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Survival, and Weaponry rolls. She loses the 10-again quality on Empathy, Expression, Persuasion, and Subterfuge rolls. <br /> Your character will leave Crescent Moon Surrender and enter Half Moon Surrender after one week. This does not give a Beat. <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Successfully resist frenzy; if so, enter New Moon Surrender. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Surrender (Half Moon)</span><br /> Subtract two dice from any roll to resist frenzy. Subtract one die from any roll to resist Detachment. Raise her effective Blood Potency by one dot. She gains the 9-again quality on all Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Survival, and Weaponry rolls. She cannot achieve exceptional successes on Empathy, Expression, Persuasion, and Subterfuge rolls, and loses 10-again. <br /> Your character will leave Half Moon Surrender and enter Gibbous Moon Surrender after one week. This does not give a Beat. <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Successfully resist frenzy; if so, enter New Moon Surrender. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Surrender (Gibbous Moon)</span><br /> Subtract three dice from any roll to resist frenzy. Subtract one die from any roll to resist Detachment. Raise her effective Blood Potency by one dot. She achieves exceptional success on three successes on all Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Survival, and Weaponry rolls, and gains 8-again. She cannot achieve exceptional successes on Empathy, Expression, Persuasion, and Subterfuge rolls, and loses 10-again. <br /> Your character will leave Gibbous Moon Surrender and enter Full Moon Surrender after one week. This does not give a Beat. <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Successfully resist frenzy; if so, enter the New Moon Surrender. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Surrender (Full Moon)</span><br /> Subtract five dice from any roll to resist frenzy. Subtract two dice from any roll to resist Detachment. Raise her effective Blood Potency by two dots. She achieves exceptional success on three successes on all Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation, Survival, and Weaponry rolls, and gains 8-again. She cannot achieve exceptional successes on Empathy, Expression, Persuasion, and Subterfuge rolls, and loses 10-again. <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Gain a dot of Humanity or enter torpor; if so, enter the New Moon Surrender. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T01:46:37-07:00","id":248701,"title":"","content":"And I love these mechanics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just a question, so BP 1 neonate drops to 0 BP with New Moon? Sounds harsh :S Same with resolution of New Moon, but waking up your beast ain't supposed to be easy. <br /> <br /> Oh, can't remember, what happens to torpor on BP 0? Do you multiply it by 0 (thus effectively, having a torpor of one night) or by 1?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T03:33:38-07:00","id":248729,"title":"","content":"Well, copying that and plastering to my WoD mechanics wall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T06:16:40-07:00","id":248772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender?p=248701#post248701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I love these mechanics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just a question, so BP 1 neonate drops to 0 BP with New Moon? Sounds harsh :S Same with resolution of New Moon, but waking up your beast ain't supposed to be easy.<br /> <br /> Oh, can't remember, what happens to torpor on BP 0? Do you multiply it by 0 (thus effectively, having a torpor of one night) or by 1?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Torpor would be rising the next night, yeah. Effectively zero nights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T06:39:44-07:00","id":248784,"title":"","content":"So for the unaware, what is this, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T06:52:38-07:00","id":248793,"title":"","content":"You mean Red Surrender? It's technique of giving partly yourself to Beast, specific to Gangrel, but at the cost of looser grip on Humanity. <br /> <br /> But I think someone more experienced will explain it better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T07:34:39-07:00","id":248833,"title":"","content":"It's a Gangrel-only benefit that first appeared in the Gangrel Clan Book. Each Clan book gave something special to each Clan (besides specific Merits and such that were par for the course). Gangrel got an expansion on their theme of being closer to their inner Beast than any other clan in the form of the Red Surrender, a sort of (but not quite) controlled Frenzy that greatly improved some skills (Athletics, Stealth, Survival and Intimidation), Initiative and rolls to avoid being ambushed and also make easier to get Exceptional successes on Animal Ken. On the bad side it penalized some skills (Academics, Computer, Medicine, Science, Empathy and Socialize), Discipline rolls involving Intelligence and increased the Untrained Penalty of Mental Skills from -3 to -4. You also couldn't regain Willpower through your Virtue.<br /> <br /> The Penalties/Bonuses started as 1 and increased by 1 (up to +/- 5) each night you remained in the Red Surrender, it also became increasignly difficult to snap out of it.<br /> <br /> The curious thing is that it felt awesome and thoroughly &quot;right&quot; to be in that state, that was the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T08:05:23-07:00","id":248871,"title":"","content":"I like the concept but I'm not sure about the resolution for new moon. Intentionally taking a character out of play seems wrong. Not sure why amaranth would &quot;help&quot; the situation. Or why loosing humanity would make you more yourself. <br /> <br /> Not sure I understand new moon at all really. Or why you would automatically default to that after the others. <br /> <br /> What if I didn't want to beat it down? Just put it back in the cage for now?<br /> <br /> How do they get into the other moon phases?<br /> You only explained how they got into crescent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","user":"overload","date":". 09-04-2014, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T08:49:57-07:00","id":248894,"title":"","content":"I like the different aspects of the beast so I figured it would be based around that if it was implemented. <br /> <br /> Something like. <br /> <br /> Uncaged:<br /> The monstrous beast has been set loose. You can feel the primal urges. Hunt, feed, survive. While in this state your beast guides your movements.<br /> Probably the effect would be something similar to crecent moon up there.<br /> <br /> Resolution would likely be entering a frenzy, or spending the usual time communing with a touchstone. <br /> <br /> Unleashed<br /> The competitive beast comes to the front challenging all who would oppose her. Gain 8 again when lashing out against threats. But they cannot back down from a threat unless they successfully make a roll to resist frenzy. <br /> <br /> Resolution. Again touchstone, or perhaps successfully fleeing a challenge. <br /> <br /> Uninhibited<br /> The seductive beast can smell desire, it can help you move like the most lithe cat. Similar I suppose to the crecent moon, except perhaps it works for some social skills. Not sure. Or maybe regain a willpower for every vessel you kill while feeding. <br /> <br /> Resolution. Eh touchstones again. Maybe have your blood potency in people to feed from willing to give the beast it's desires. Or killing a number of vessels equal to your blood potency. <br /> <br /> <br /> Dunno. I just expected something more along those lines. Since the aspects of the beast were already built into the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","user":"overload","date":". 09-04-2014, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:51:06-07:00","id":248970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender?p=248871#post248871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the concept but I'm not sure about the resolution for new moon. Intentionally taking a character out of play seems wrong. Not sure why amaranth would &quot;help&quot; the situation. Or why loosing humanity would make you more yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of agree, it makes it VERY difficult to break out of the cycle. I guess that's the point, but I do wish there was a way to end it that didn't put you at a huge risk of having to retire your character.<br /> <br /> On the bright side, with the bonus it grants to resist Frenzy, you should have a pretty easy time getting back to Crescent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure I understand new moon at all really. Or why you would automatically default to that after the others. <br /> <br /> What if I didn't want to beat it down? Just put it back in the cage for now? </div> </div> </div>What if I don't want to get a hangover? Sucks for me. Part of entering any altered state of consciousness is the backlash afterwards as your brain chemistry (or in this case, your humanity) tries to compensate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do they get into the other moon phases?<br /> You only explained how they got into crescent. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Your character will leave Crescent Moon Surrender and enter Half Moon Surrender after one week. This does not grant a Beat.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's no way to skip straight to a higher stage, you have to start out in Crescent Moon and work your way up to Full over the course of 4 weeks (by not successfully resisting Frenzy during that time).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-04-2014, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T12:20:55-07:00","id":249058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender?p=248970#post248970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if I don't want to get a hangover? Sucks for me. Part of entering any altered state of consciousness is the backlash afterwards as your brain chemistry (or in this case, your humanity) </div> </div> </div> </div>Sure you can. Just drink orange juice n water before you pass out. Always seems to work for me with patron\u00e8 shots. Lol.<br /> <br /> But seriously not saying it should be easy. <br /> <br /> Just not sure how this in particular makes sense. I could understand reaching a breaking point allowing you the option of coming out of it. But automatically requiring things like humanity loss or torpor is too steep. <br /> <br /> It should feel good, IE gaining willpower for feeding the beast. On top of the other benefits.<br /> <br /> Perhaps tell the players each time they hit a breaking point but the ST rolls in secret the actual results. So you don't feel bad for the actions till you decide to come out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T13:50:59-07:00","id":249143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender?p=249058#post249058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure you can. Just drink orange juice n water before you pass out. Always seems to work for me with patron\u00e8 shots. Lol.<br /> <br /> But seriously not saying it should be easy. <br /> <br /> Just not sure how this in particular makes sense. I could understand reaching a breaking point allowing you the option of coming out of it. But automatically requiring things like humanity loss or torpor is too steep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it doesn't require that unless you want to get completely out of the Red Surrender Cycle. With the +5 New Moon gives you on rolls to resist Frenzy, you could always just singe yourself with a lighter or something for a Frenzy trigger and you'd have a pretty good chance of resisting, thereby putting you back into Crecent Moon. It does say you can choose to take Crescent Moon <i>any time</i> you successfully resist Frenzy, and I'd assume you can't have New Moon and Crescent Moon simultaneously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T16:47:45-07:00","id":249286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender?p=249058#post249058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure you can. Just drink orange juice n water before you pass out. Always seems to work for me with patron\u00e8 shots. Lol.<br /> <br /> But seriously not saying it should be easy.<br /> <br /> Just not sure how this in particular makes sense. I could understand reaching a breaking point allowing you the option of coming out of it. But automatically requiring things like humanity loss or torpor is too steep.<br /> <br /> It should feel good, IE gaining willpower for feeding the beast. On top of the other benefits.<br /> <br /> Perhaps tell the players each time they hit a breaking point but the ST rolls in secret the actual results. So you don't feel bad for the actions till you decide to come out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If that works better for you, great. Just posting notes from my chronicle. My players haven't had problems with it so far. But then again, they live for steep risks and costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T17:44:46-07:00","id":249323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender?p=248833#post248833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a Gangrel-only benefit that first appeared in the Gangrel Clan Book. Each Clan book gave something special to each Clan (besides specific Merits and such that were par for the course). Gangrel got an expansion on their theme of being closer to their inner Beast than any other clan in the form of the Red Surrender, a sort of (but not quite) controlled Frenzy that greatly improved some skills (Athletics, Stealth, Survival and Intimidation), Initiative and rolls to avoid being ambushed and also make easier to get Exceptional successes on Animal Ken. On the bad side it penalized some skills (Academics, Computer, Medicine, Science, Empathy and Socialize), Discipline rolls involving Intelligence and increased the Untrained Penalty of Mental Skills from -3 to -4. You also couldn't regain Willpower through your Virtue.<br /> <br /> The Penalties/Bonuses started as 1 and increased by 1 (up to +/- 5) each night you remained in the Red Surrender, it also became increasignly difficult to snap out of it.<br /> <br /> The curious thing is that it felt awesome and thoroughly &quot;right&quot; to be in that state, that was the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was an optional inverse mechanic geared toward keeping your human side at the cost of of suppressing the beast as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T17:47:16-07:00","id":249325,"title":"","content":"Yeah. This is just how I come up with ideas. Not telling ya how to do yours. I just like having a place to bounce ideas around. <br /> <br /> My other post is what I was hoping to get more feedback on. Granted it's barely even a concept. <br /> <br /> But basing the red surrender off the already implemented aspects of the beast seems like it would be more thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> Also one default rule I thought should apply to all aspects is you can't fight in stun or beat down. The beast plays for keeps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T13:17:20-07:00","id":709201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248635-b-s-red-surrender?p=248894#post248894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the different aspects of the beast so I figured it would be based around that if it was implemented.<br /> <br /> Uncaged [...] Unleashed [...] Uninhibited [...] Dunno. I just expected something more along those lines. Since the aspects of the beast were already built into the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like MachineIV's concept (though if I use it there might be some minor alterations), but you have a good point by bringing up the idea of Uncaged, Unleashed, and Uninhibited.<br /> <br /> The Beast does have its aspects; in its untrammeled form it's mindless, instinctive\u2014as the text goes, <i>Hunt, kill, feed, sleep. Repeat.\u2014</i>but the Red Surrender is filtering it through the rationale of the Human to an extent.<br /> <br /> Instead of it being a sliding scale like the moon phase version, maybe one could opt to take a Persistent version of a predatory aura condition (or something similar to your ideas here, or bits of both), in exchange for a few related bonuses. One could even combine all three conditions, depending on how much you want to surrender. (And if they were indeed separate from Bestial/Competitive/Wanton, someone who was in Surrender would be a hell of a thing to try to push an Aura on, win lose OR draw.)<br /> <br /> Granted, someone who was under all three aspects of Surrender would basically be a narcissistic sociopath on a massive coke binge, but that'd be part of the fun, yeh?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 10-19-2015, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}